{
    "type": "game",
    "name": "Stories From the Cores",
    "steam_appid": 2202340,
    "required_age": 0,
    "is_free": true,
    "detailed_description": "<div class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2202340/extras/af3dfe9a72b56e93917ff77c3ea12b70.avif?t=1682455946\" /></div><br><br>Deep beneath the ocean floor, what discoveries are possible? Join<br>science bot Rovee on 3 expeditions with the International Ocean<br>Discovery Project. Drill core samples from below the ocean floor,<br>compare the layers, investigate hypotheses, and piece together<br>dramatic stories of life on Earth.<br><br>Stores from the Cores is a suite of 3 single-player mini games about<br>deep ocean core science. The games feature multiple choice questions, <br>exploring 3D environments with science bot Rovee via point and <br>click controls. Collecting mineral samples for scientific research, and <br>matching games that all teach players about deep ocean core science. <br><br>\u201cIt\u2019s like a fun game and you can learn from it.\u201d  Age 12<br><br>The mini games are the following:<br><br><strong>Mysteries of the Core </strong><br>Why are bits of land plants found in cores drilled from<br>under the sea floor far from shore?<br><br>\u201cIt's a colorful, interesting story, connected to what science is finding out.\u201d Age 40<br><div class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2202340/extras/64ca766f8e85cf9086fa5d92280b72a3.avif?t=1682455946\" /></div><br><br><br><strong>Deep Dark Life </strong><br>How are microbes able to live inside rocks hundreds of feet below<br>the sea floor? Find out what the Center for Dark Energy Biosphere Investigations<br>has discovered.<br><br>\u201cI never thought of microbes at the bottom of the sea. I thought it was a<br>dark place with nothing going on.\u201d Age 40s<br><br><div class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2202340/extras/cec5391e0baeb6d11d79785c1c815096.avif?t=1682455946\" /></div><br><br><strong>Die-no-saur</strong><br>What do dinosaurs and plankton have in common? What happened<br>on Earth when dinosaurs, plankton and lots of other life went extinct?<br><br>\u201cOcean drilling means\u2026getting samples from the ground to play back<br>history to find out what happened.\u201d Age 14<br><div class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2202340/extras/965a7daffa109359c03c0b69901fc7cd.avif?t=1682455946\" /></div><br><br><strong>Accuracy</strong><br>These games are based on current scientific data. HOWEVER, we did add googley eyes to the microbes. <br><div class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2202340/extras/fc967e796f20e2fa6f9d1f26df075033.avif?t=1682455946\" /></div><br><br><br><strong>Funding from</strong><br>This project is funded through National Science Foundation Award #1515856 and the Center for<br>Dark Energy Biosphere Investigations.",
    "about_the_game": "<div class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2202340/extras/af3dfe9a72b56e93917ff77c3ea12b70.avif?t=1682455946\" /></div><br><br>Deep beneath the ocean floor, what discoveries are possible? Join<br>science bot Rovee on 3 expeditions with the International Ocean<br>Discovery Project. Drill core samples from below the ocean floor,<br>compare the layers, investigate hypotheses, and piece together<br>dramatic stories of life on Earth.<br><br>Stores from the Cores is a suite of 3 single-player mini games about<br>deep ocean core science. The games feature multiple choice questions, <br>exploring 3D environments with science bot Rovee via point and <br>click controls. Collecting mineral samples for scientific research, and <br>matching games that all teach players about deep ocean core science. <br><br>\u201cIt\u2019s like a fun game and you can learn from it.\u201d  Age 12<br><br>The mini games are the following:<br><br><strong>Mysteries of the Core </strong><br>Why are bits of land plants found in cores drilled from<br>under the sea floor far from shore?<br><br>\u201cIt's a colorful, interesting story, connected to what science is finding out.\u201d Age 40<br><div class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2202340/extras/64ca766f8e85cf9086fa5d92280b72a3.avif?t=1682455946\" /></div><br><br><br><strong>Deep Dark Life </strong><br>How are microbes able to live inside rocks hundreds of feet below<br>the sea floor? Find out what the Center for Dark Energy Biosphere Investigations<br>has discovered.<br><br>\u201cI never thought of microbes at the bottom of the sea. I thought it was a<br>dark place with nothing going on.\u201d Age 40s<br><br><div class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2202340/extras/cec5391e0baeb6d11d79785c1c815096.avif?t=1682455946\" /></div><br><br><strong>Die-no-saur</strong><br>What do dinosaurs and plankton have in common? What happened<br>on Earth when dinosaurs, plankton and lots of other life went extinct?<br><br>\u201cOcean drilling means\u2026getting samples from the ground to play back<br>history to find out what happened.\u201d Age 14<br><div class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2202340/extras/965a7daffa109359c03c0b69901fc7cd.avif?t=1682455946\" /></div><br><br><strong>Accuracy</strong><br>These games are based on current scientific data. HOWEVER, we did add googley eyes to the microbes. <br><div class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2202340/extras/fc967e796f20e2fa6f9d1f26df075033.avif?t=1682455946\" /></div><br><br><br><strong>Funding from</strong><br>This project is funded through National Science Foundation Award #1515856 and the Center for<br>Dark Energy Biosphere Investigations.",
